  "presentation_summary": [
    "73-year-old man with lung adenocarcinoma developed AIHA after 13 cycles of pembrolizumab.",
    "Relevant history included COPD, hypertension, atrial fibrillation, prior bilateral cataract surgery, former smoking, and multiple chronic medications.",
    "At AIHA presentation, hemoglobin dropped from 110 to 74 g/L and total bilirubin rose from 18 to 88 umol/L.",
    "WBC was 18.7 x10^9/L, neutrophils 11.09 x10^9/L, and platelets 532 x10^9/L.",
    "LDH was 1615 U/L, reticulocytes 590 x10^9/L, haptoglobin <0.30 g/L, and DAT was positive.",
    "Pembrolizumab was stopped; he received prednisolone 1 mg/kg, folic acid, omeprazole, two units RBC, and antibiotics for possible lower respiratory tract infection, with clinical improvement."
  ],
